 #, no-javascript-format
 msgid ""
 "<p>Open a note or task and tap Print to use its current draft. Android "
@@ -17179,3 +16993,429 @@ msgstr "À propos de ce projet"
 #. Complete versus partial snapshot restoration, Refs #824.
 msgid "<p class='achtung'><b>All always uses the replace method.</b> Changes made after the selected snapshot are overwritten and entries added later are removed. The additive method is available only for individual areas.</p>"
 msgstr "<p class='achtung'><b>Tout utilise toujours la méthode de remplacement.</b> Les modifications postérieures à l’instantané sélectionné sont écrasées et les entrées ajoutées depuis sont supprimées. La méthode additive est réservée aux domaines individuels.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: android-apk-transfer, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<div class='download-karten'><figure class='download-karte'><a "
+"href='https://gitlab.com/maik3531/mint-forgs/-/raw/main/Magnolie-"
+"Organitzer/Magnolie-Notes.apk'><img class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='Magnolie Notes'><figcaption><b>Magnolie Notes</b><br>Magnolie-"
+"Notes.apk<br>gitlab.com</figcaption></a></figure><figure class='download-"
+"karte'><a "
+"href='https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.kde.kdeconnect_tp'><img"
+" class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='KDE Connect'><figcaption><b>KDE Connect</b><br>Google "
+"Play</figcaption></a></figure></div><p><a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>Magnolie"
+" Notes · F-Droid</a></p><p>Alternatively, install and update Notes through "
+"the F-Droid client. F-Droid recommends its client: downloading an APK from "
+"its website alone provides no update notifications and is less secure. The "
+"APK transfer and checksum steps above describe the direct project download, "
+"not F-Droid. Versions and signing certificates can differ between channels. "
+"Back up your data before changing channels; do not uninstall an existing app"
+" to bypass a signature mismatch.</p><p>In the prepared Notes update, About "
+"refers recognized F-Droid installations and F-Droid builds to the client "
+"instead of offering a GitHub update. Android may not retain the installer "
+"information; a manually downloaded APK does not reliably identify its "
+"website. If recognition is unavailable, follow the conditional F-Droid "
+"reminder when that was your source. This recognition is not a signature "
+"check.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<div class='download-karten'><figure class='download-karte'><a "
+"href='https://gitlab.com/maik3531/mint-forgs/-/raw/main/Magnolie-"
+"Organitzer/Magnolie-Notes.apk'><img class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='Magnolie Notes'><figcaption><b>Magnolie Notes</b><br>Magnolie-"
+"Notes.apk<br>gitlab.com</figcaption></a></figure><figure class='download-"
+"karte'><a "
+"href='https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.kde.kdeconnect_tp'><img"
+" class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='KDE Connect'><figcaption><b>KDE Connect</b><br>Google "
+"Play</figcaption></a></figure></div><p><a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>Magnolie"
+" Notes · F-Droid</a></p><p>Installez et mettez à jour Notes avec le client "
+"F-Droid. Télécharger uniquement un APK du site ne fournit aucune "
+"notification de mise à jour. Les versions et signatures peuvent différer ; "
+"sauvegardez avant de changer de source et ne désinstallez pas l’application "
+"pour contourner un conflit de signature.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: maps-routes-and-messages, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>Choose the destination address</h3><p>If several destinations are "
+"available, <b>Map</b> opens <b>Choose an address</b>: select a home, work or"
+" other address on the card, or an address of a named emergency contact. "
+"Labels include the person and relationship. A missing linked card is not "
+"offered. A single destination opens directly. <b>Cancel</b> opens no "
+"destination and changes no contact data. Your map service, route setting and"
+" saved sender address under <b>Settings ▸ Contacts</b> still apply; a route "
+"needs your own address as its starting point.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>Choisir l’adresse de destination</h3><p>Avec plusieurs destinations, "
+"<b>Carte</b> ouvre le choix d’adresse : sélectionnez une adresse privée, "
+"professionnelle ou autre de la fiche, ou celle d’un contact d’urgence nommé."
+" Le libellé indique la personne et sa relation. Une fiche liée manquante "
+"n’est pas proposée. Une destination unique s’ouvre directement. "
+"<b>Annuler</b> n’ouvre aucune destination et ne modifie aucun contact. Le "
+"service cartographique, le mode itinéraire et l’adresse d’expéditeur des "
+"<b>Paramètres ▸ Contacts</b> restent applicables ; un itinéraire exige votre"
+" adresse comme départ.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: phone-pairing, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>Confirm once at the counterpart</h3><p>Enable the phone connection and "
+"open Notes and Organizer on the same Wi-Fi. Start pairing and select the "
+"intended device. Both screens show the six-digit code. Compare it and press "
+"<b>Codes match</b> only on the other device. The initiating device displays "
+"the code and offers Cancel; no second approval is needed there. A desktop "
+"invitation is confirmed in Notes; a Notes request is confirmed on the "
+"desktop.</p><p>Wait for the connected status. Existing encryption and finish"
+" verification remain in use. Choose synchronization, contact and phone-"
+"function grants separately. Bluetooth data requires supported hardware and "
+"OS permissions; Wi-Fi remains preferred, and call audio is "
+"separate.</p><h3>Pair again after removal</h3><p>If the desktop removes a "
+"connected pairing, Notes forgets that relationship too. If the phone was "
+"offline, accept a fresh pairing request for the same computer and compare "
+"the new code; no manual forgetting is required first. Cancelling before "
+"confirmation keeps the saved pairing. Completing renewal replaces only that "
+"computer’s connection data; notes, tasks and other saved computers "
+"remain.</p><h3>Scope and permissions</h3><p>Each Organizer binds exactly one"
+" pinned own phone through <b>magnolie-phone/1</b>. This is separate from a "
+"Magnolienbaum branch and from KDE Connect. Notes can keep several paired "
+"computers and selects one active computer. Wi-Fi is available on Linux and "
+"Windows. Supported devices can use RFCOMM manually; missing OS permission, "
+"hardware or radio access may instead report <b>permission_missing</b>, "
+"<b>no_hardware</b>, <b>disabled</b> or <b>os_restricted</b>. This data "
+"channel carries no call audio.</p><p>Device status, read-only selected app "
+"notifications, contact reading and call actions have granular permissions. "
+"Choose them explicitly; pairing alone does not enable them. Notes and task "
+"synchronization use their shared preferences, and automatic Wi-Fi mode stays"
+" Wi-Fi only.</p><h3>Developer options and Notes diagnostics</h3><p>In "
+"Settings → About, click the version number on the left ten times. The "
+"additional Developer options tab contains Keep a troubleshooting log, Show "
+"log and Disable developer mode. Disabling also turns off the optional log. "
+"In Notes settings, tap the installed version ten times, open Debug options "
+"and enable WLAN debugging. Read Notes WLAN diagnostics on the desktop reads "
+"the version and up to 128 technical connection events through the confirmed "
+"own phone’s encrypted Wi-Fi session. Both sides must allow device status. "
+"Disabling Notes developer mode revokes WLAN debugging. Bluetooth cannot read"
+" this report.</p><h3>Phone filesystem in the file manager</h3><p>Under "
+"<b>Settings → KDE Connect</b>, <b>Phone name filesystem</b> opens the "
+"folders shared by the phone, using its actual name. The button appears only "
+"with a current confirmed Wi-Fi connection and available filesystem support; "
+"it disappears after disconnection, with Bluetooth alone or without a client."
+" Share storage locations in KDE Connect on the phone. The direct Linux "
+"connection needs SSHFS and fusermount; Windows needs existing SSHFS-Win and "
+"WinFsp. Existing system KDE Connect uses its own filesystem facility. The "
+"counterpart is checked again before opening.</p><p>Windows Setup offers the "
+"phone-filesystem components and, when needed, installs the bundled signed "
+"WinFsp/SSHFS-Win packages with one administrator approval. In the portable "
+"edition, run <code>filesystem-runtime/Telefon-Dateisystem "
+"vorbereiten.cmd</code>. Existing components are retained and are not removed"
+" when uninstalling Organizer. Reading status or opening the filesystem never"
+" installs components.</p><p>KDE Connect offers assigned music/video players "
+"and other active playback, including browser videos. In Settings → "
+"Magnolienbaum → Media players, Search/Open uses the system file chooser, "
+"separately for music and video. Linux also shows searchable titles/artists "
+"when the assigned player exposes MPRIS TrackList; Windows GSMTC exposes "
+"current playback, not a music library. The phone displays actual covers and "
+"optional shuffle/repeat when supported. Streaming-service catalog searches "
+"require that service’s own application.</p><h3>Linux: Receive folders for "
+"photos and videos</h3><p>With your own Magnolie Notes phone connected over "
+"Wi-Fi, open <b>Settings ▸ Magnolie Notes phone connection ▸ Advanced "
+"functions ▸ Photos and videos</b>. No folder selection is needed before "
+"switching on synchronization. By default, photos go to <i>Pictures/&lt;phone"
+" name&gt;-Fotos</i> in your system’s Pictures folder. If you separately "
+"enable <b>Also synchronize videos</b>, videos use <i>Videos/&lt;phone "
+"name&gt;-Videos</i> in your system’s Videos folder. The video option starts "
+"off.</p><p>Choose <b>Photos · Destination folder</b> or <b>Videos · "
+"Destination folder</b> only to use a different folder for that media type. "
+"Leave the corresponding switch off while choosing. The folder must belong to"
+" you and not be writable by other users, including via a group. If the "
+"standard path is rejected, the Organizer does not change permissions or "
+"switch to another folder on its own. Choosing another folder alone does not "
+"grant Android media access, transfer or move files, or activate "
+"synchronization.</p><p>When shared media settings are available, their "
+"on/off switch is in the <b>Photos and videos</b> heading. Opening the "
+"section does not turn anything on. The local <b>Receive · Photos</b> "
+"permission is separate inside the section.</p><p>After opening an already "
+"saved book, you do not need to save it again just to choose a "
+"folder.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, a new default destination uses your "
+"account name only when the phone name is missing. If the phone name is just "
+"an emoji, for example, the default folders are <i>Telefon-Fotos</i> and "
+"<i>Telefon-Videos</i>. Already saved destination folders stay "
+"unchanged.</p><p><b>Restore</b> is under <b>Photos and videos</b>, after the"
+" destination folders and before <b>Synchronize now</b>. Local media versions"
+" can be restored without an active phone connection. On Linux and Windows, "
+"this section shows the same recycle-bin policy as under Security. For "
+"example, choose 30 days or <b>never – empty manually</b>. Your existing "
+"choice is preserved. Switching the recycle bin off does not empty it. Use "
+"<b>Delete permanently</b> for one entry. <b>Empty recycle bin</b> asks you "
+"to confirm the number of all eligible media items in the displayed local "
+"bin; on Windows, choose <b>Read media recycle bin</b> first. Originals not "
+"yet moved into the bin are kept. If emptying fails, refresh the list first; "
+"some items may already have been deleted.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, "
+"<b>Advanced functions</b> is only shown while Notes is connected over Wi-Fi."
+" Without that connection, look for <b>Restore media</b> separately under "
+"<b>Magnolie Notes phone connection</b>; on Windows it appears for a paired "
+"device with a local backup.</p><p>In Magnolie Notes, <b>Restore</b> is under"
+" <b>Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b> when connected over Wi-Fi. "
+"Existing local copies remain available in the Journal even when "
+"disconnected. Your gallery app manages the recycle bin for phone originals "
+"and its retention period (for example, 30 days). Empty that bin in the "
+"gallery app, not in the list of recovery copies in Notes.</p><p>Contact "
+"synchronization adds messenger destinations. The same WhatsApp or Signal "
+"number is not added again for that service, even if formatted differently. "
+"The same applies to a matching Threema ID. Existing formatting and custom "
+"actions are kept; different numbers, IDs and services remain "
+"separate.</p><p>Drawing tablet: KDE Connect sends position, contact, "
+"pressure and Pen/Rubber changes. Magnolie uses these in the active sheet, "
+"including the Notes drawing dialog. The visible hover cursor leaves no "
+"stroke and is not saved or exported. The phone menu offers fullscreen and "
+"settings to hide the finger-drawing button or place it in any corner. Pen "
+"variants, shapes, selection, zoom and undo belong to Magnolie’s toolbar. "
+"Tilt, pen rotation and extra pen buttons are not part of this KDE "
+"protocol.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>Confirmer une seule fois sur l’autre appareil</h3><p>Activez la "
+"connexion et ouvrez Notes et Organizer sur le même Wi-Fi. Lancez "
+"l’association et choisissez l’appareil. Comparez les six chiffres affichés "
+"des deux côtés, puis confirmez seulement sur l’autre appareil : dans Notes "
+"pour une invitation du PC, sur le PC pour une demande de Notes. L’appareil "
+"de départ affiche le code et permet d’annuler. Attendez l’état connecté ; "
+"les autorisations restent séparées.</p><p>Une suppression transmise par la "
+"connexion authentifiée retire aussi l’association dans Notes. Si le "
+"téléphone était hors ligne, acceptez une nouvelle demande du même PC sans "
+"supprimer d’abord l’ancienne association. Annuler avant confirmation la "
+"conserve ; terminer la remplace sans effacer notes, tâches ni autres PC. "
+"Bluetooth nécessite le matériel et les permissions pris en charge et ne "
+"transporte pas l’audio des appels.</p><h3>Options de développement et "
+"diagnostic Notes</h3><p>Dans Paramètres → À propos, cliquez dix fois sur la "
+"version à gauche. Le nouvel onglet de développement contient le journal de "
+"dépannage, son affichage et la désactivation du mode. Désactiver coupe aussi"
+" le journal facultatif. Dans les paramètres Notes, touchez dix fois la "
+"version installée, ouvrez les options de débogage et activez le débogage Wi-"
+"Fi. Le diagnostic Notes sur le PC lit la version et au plus 128 événements "
+"techniques via la session Wi-Fi chiffrée du téléphone personnel confirmé. "
+"Les deux côtés doivent autoriser l’état de l’appareil. Désactiver le mode "
+"dans Notes révoque le débogage Wi-Fi. Bluetooth ne permet pas cette "
+"lecture.</p><h3>Fichiers du téléphone</h3><p>Dans <b>Paramètres → KDE "
+"Connect</b>, <b>Système de fichiers du téléphone</b> affiche son nom réel et"
+" ouvre les dossiers partagés dans le gestionnaire de fichiers. Le bouton "
+"apparaît uniquement avec une connexion Wi-Fi confirmée active et la fonction"
+" disponible. Il disparaît après déconnexion, avec Bluetooth seul ou sans "
+"client. Autorisez les dossiers dans KDE Connect sur le téléphone. La "
+"connexion directe Linux nécessite SSHFS et fusermount ; Windows nécessite "
+"SSHFS-Win et WinFsp. KDE Connect système utilise sa propre fonction. "
+"L’appareil est vérifié avant l’ouverture.</p><p>Le programme d’installation "
+"Windows propose les composants du système de fichiers du téléphone et "
+"installe au besoin les paquets WinFsp/SSHFS-Win signés fournis, avec une "
+"autorisation administrateur unique. Pour la version portable, lancez "
+"<code>filesystem-runtime/Telefon-Dateisystem vorbereiten.cmd</code>. Les "
+"composants existants sont conservés, même après désinstallation d’Organizer."
+" La lecture de l’état et l’ouverture des fichiers n’installent aucun "
+"composant.</p><p>KDE Connect propose les lecteurs attribués et les lectures "
+"actives, y compris les vidéos du navigateur. Dans Paramètres → Magnolienbaum"
+" → Lecteurs multimédias, Rechercher/Ouvrir utilise le sélecteur système, "
+"séparément pour musique et vidéo. Linux affiche aussi une recherche de "
+"titres/artistes si le lecteur expose MPRIS TrackList ; Windows GSMTC fournit"
+" la lecture actuelle, pas de bibliothèque. Le téléphone montre les pochettes"
+" et les modes aléatoire/répétition pris en charge. Les catalogues de "
+"streaming se recherchent dans leur propre application.</p><h3>Linux: Receive"
+" folders for photos and videos</h3><p>With your own Magnolie Notes phone "
+"connected over Wi-Fi, open <b>Settings ▸ Magnolie Notes phone connection ▸ "
+"Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b>. No folder selection is needed "
+"before switching on synchronization. By default, photos go to "
+"<i>Pictures/&lt;phone name&gt;-Fotos</i> in your system’s Pictures folder. "
+"If you separately enable <b>Also synchronize videos</b>, videos use "
+"<i>Videos/&lt;phone name&gt;-Videos</i> in your system’s Videos folder. The "
+"video option starts off.</p><p>Choose <b>Photos · Destination folder</b> or "
+"<b>Videos · Destination folder</b> only to use a different folder for that "
+"media type. Leave the corresponding switch off while choosing. The folder "
+"must belong to you and not be writable by other users, including via a "
+"group. If the standard path is rejected, the Organizer does not change "
+"permissions or switch to another folder on its own. Choosing another folder "
+"alone does not grant Android media access, transfer or move files, or "
+"activate synchronization.</p><p>When shared media settings are available, "
+"their on/off switch is in the <b>Photos and videos</b> heading. Opening the "
+"section does not turn anything on. The local <b>Receive · Photos</b> "
+"permission is separate inside the section.</p><p>After opening an already "
+"saved book, you do not need to save it again just to choose a "
+"folder.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, a new default destination uses your "
+"account name only when the phone name is missing. If the phone name is just "
+"an emoji, for example, the default folders are <i>Telefon-Fotos</i> and "
+"<i>Telefon-Videos</i>. Already saved destination folders stay "
+"unchanged.</p><p><b>Restore</b> is under <b>Photos and videos</b>, after the"
+" destination folders and before <b>Synchronize now</b>. Local media versions"
+" can be restored without an active phone connection. On Linux and Windows, "
+"this section shows the same recycle-bin policy as under Security. For "
+"example, choose 30 days or <b>never – empty manually</b>. Your existing "
+"choice is preserved. Switching the recycle bin off does not empty it. Use "
+"<b>Delete permanently</b> for one entry. <b>Empty recycle bin</b> asks you "
+"to confirm the number of all eligible media items in the displayed local "
+"bin; on Windows, choose <b>Read media recycle bin</b> first. Originals not "
+"yet moved into the bin are kept. If emptying fails, refresh the list first; "
+"some items may already have been deleted.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, "
+"<b>Advanced functions</b> is only shown while Notes is connected over Wi-Fi."
+" Without that connection, look for <b>Restore media</b> separately under "
+"<b>Magnolie Notes phone connection</b>; on Windows it appears for a paired "
+"device with a local backup.</p><p>In Magnolie Notes, <b>Restore</b> is under"
+" <b>Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b> when connected over Wi-Fi. "
+"Existing local copies remain available in the Journal even when "
+"disconnected. Your gallery app manages the recycle bin for phone originals "
+"and its retention period (for example, 30 days). Empty that bin in the "
+"gallery app, not in the list of recovery copies in Notes.</p><p>Tablette "
+"graphique : KDE Connect transmet position, contact, pression et changement "
+"stylet/gomme. Magnolie les utilise dans la feuille active, y compris le "
+"dessin d’une note. Le curseur de survol ne dessine pas et n’est ni "
+"enregistré ni exporté. Le menu du téléphone offre plein écran et réglages "
+"pour masquer le bouton de dessin au doigt ou le placer dans un coin. Les "
+"variantes de stylet, formes, sélection, zoom et annulation appartiennent à "
+"Magnolie. Inclinaison, rotation et boutons supplémentaires ne font pas "
+"partie de ce protocole KDE.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: contact-details-and-anniversaries, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>Contact groups</h3><p><b>Settings ▸ Contacts ▸ Contact "
+"groups</b></p><p><b>More fields</b>: Family · Work · Client · Tradesperson ·"
+" Insurance · Doctor</p><p><b>Add contact group</b></p><h3>Exclude selected "
+"groups</h3><p>Open Settings → Notifications → Exclude contact groups. Choose"
+" Notifications, Anniversaries, Appointment overview or Print, then Birthdays"
+" only, All anniversaries, Appointments or All. Tick the specific contact "
+"groups: other groups remain unaffected. Each area keeps its own choices. "
+"Enable exclusions and save. For the overview, Also hide in the calendar is "
+"optional. Appointment rules use linked contacts; for synchronized work "
+"appointments without a contact, explicitly select their calendar. During "
+"vacation, you can suppress notifications while retaining the display, or "
+"hide the entries too. Print has separate choices, including contact cards. "
+"You can change or disable the rules at any time; disabling retains the "
+"choices. No contacts, appointments or provider data are deleted.</p><h3>Find"
+" a contact group</h3><p>Above the contact list, Contact groups offers All, "
+"No contact group and individual groups, including empty standard groups. A "
+"selected group searches across all alphabet tabs and combines with the "
+"search text. Selecting an alphabet tab returns to All and ordinary alphabet "
+"browsing. Filtering never changes memberships or provider "
+"data.</p><h3>Complete emergency contacts</h3><p>Under <b>More fields ▸ "
+"Emergency contacts</b>, add a named person and relationship. <b>Link "
+"existing contact</b> shows the current card’s details read-only: photo, "
+"company, phone numbers, email and postal addresses, dates, notes and social "
+"media. Edit the linked card to change them. Choosing <b>— do not link —</b> "
+"keeps the displayed details as an independent, editable copy. Changes in the"
+" editor apply only with <b>Save</b>; <b>Cancel</b> leaves the saved contacts"
+" unchanged.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>Groupes de contacts</h3><p><b>Paramètres ▸ Contacts ▸ Groupes de "
+"contacts</b></p><p><b>Autres champs</b>: Famille · Travail · Client · "
+"Artisan · Assurance · Médecin</p><p><b>Ajouter un groupe de "
+"contacts</b></p><h3>Exclure les groupes choisis</h3><p>Ouvrez Paramètres → "
+"Notifications → Exclure des groupes de contacts. Choisissez Notifications, "
+"Dates anniversaires, Aperçu des rendez-vous ou Imprimer, puis Naissances "
+"uniquement, Toutes les dates anniversaires, Rendez-vous ou Tous. Cochez les "
+"groupes précis ; les autres restent inchangés. Chaque domaine conserve ses "
+"choix. Activez et enregistrez. Masquer aussi dans le calendrier est "
+"facultatif. Les rendez-vous utilisent les contacts liés ; sélectionnez "
+"explicitement le calendrier des rendez-vous professionnels synchronisés sans"
+" contact. En vacances, désactivez leurs notifications et, si souhaité, leur "
+"affichage. L’impression possède ses propres choix, y compris pour les "
+"fiches. Modifiez ou désactivez les règles à tout moment ; les choix sont "
+"conservés. Aucune donnée n’est supprimée.</p><h3>Trouver un groupe de "
+"contacts</h3><p>Au-dessus de la liste, Groupes de contacts propose Tous, "
+"Aucun groupe et chaque groupe, même les groupes standard vides. Le groupe "
+"choisi est recherché dans tous les onglets alphabétiques et combiné au texte"
+" de recherche. Choisir une lettre rétablit Tous et la navigation "
+"alphabétique. Le filtrage ne modifie ni appartenances ni données des "
+"fournisseurs.</p><h3>Contacts d’urgence complets</h3><p>Dans <b>Autres "
+"champs ▸ Contacts d’urgence</b>, ajoutez une personne nommée et sa relation."
+" <b>Lier un contact existant</b> affiche les données actuelles de sa fiche "
+"en lecture seule : photo, société, téléphones, adresses électroniques et "
+"postales, dates, notes et réseaux sociaux. Modifiez la fiche liée pour les "
+"changer. <b>— ne pas lier —</b> conserve les données affichées comme copie "
+"indépendante modifiable. Seul <b>Enregistrer</b> applique le brouillon ; "
+"<b>Annuler</b> laisse les contacts enregistrés inchangés.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: welcome, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>One page number, several screen sections</h3><p>A numbered handbook page"
+" may fill several screen sections, depending on your screen resolution and "
+"window size. Seeing the same page number again as you turn forward is "
+"intentional: no pages are missing or duplicated. The number identifies the "
+"fixed handbook page, so the contents and topic links always refer to the "
+"same page, even after resizing the window.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>Un numéro, plusieurs écrans</h3><p>Selon la résolution et la taille de "
+"la fenêtre, une page numérotée du manuel peut occuper plusieurs écrans. "
+"Revoir le même numéro en avançant est normal : aucune page ne manque ni "
+"n’est en double. Le numéro désigne la page fixe du manuel ; le sommaire et "
+"les liens thématiques renvoient toujours à cette même page, même après "
+"redimensionnement.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: turning-pages-and-moving-around, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p class='kalender-blaettertasten'><kbd>&larr;</kbd> / <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> · "
+"Use the left and right arrow keys to turn one month, one week or two days, "
+"depending on the Calendar view. If a date or time cell has focus, the keys "
+"move focus instead. In text fields, they move the cursor.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p class='kalender-blaettertasten'><kbd>&larr;</kbd> / <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> · "
+"Les flèches gauche et droite font défiler le calendrier d’un mois, d’une "
+"semaine ou de deux jours selon la vue. Si une cellule de date ou d’heure a "
+"le focus, les flèches déplacent ce focus. Dans un champ de texte, elles "
+"déplacent le curseur.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: the-appimage, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p>Magnolie Organizer is also listed in the <a "
+"href='https://appimage.github.io/Magnolie-Organizer'>AppImage catalogue</a>."
+" This is a catalogue entry; check the linked release and its checksum before"
+" running an AppImage.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p><a href='https://appimage.github.io/Magnolie-Organizer'>AppImage · "
+"Magnolie Organizer</a></p><p>Magnolie Organizer figure aussi dans le "
+"catalogue AppImage. Vérifiez la version liée et sa somme de contrôle avant "
+"de la lancer.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: first-run-assistant, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p>On the phone-apps page, <b>Magnolie Notes · F-Droid</b> opens <a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>the "
+"F-Droid listing</a> as an alternative to the direct APK download. Opening "
+"the link does not install the app or grant phone permissions.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p><a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>Magnolie"
+" Notes · F-Droid</a></p><p>La page des applications du téléphone de "
+"l’assistant propose Magnolie Notes · F-Droid comme alternative à l’APK "
+"direct. Ouvrir le lien n’installe rien et n’accorde aucune autorisation du "
+"téléphone.</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: moving-from-lotus-organizer, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p>Open Settings → Import → <b>Lotus Organizer (.or6 / .csv) …</b> and "
+"select an OR6 file or CSV export. OR6 imports appointments, tasks, contacts "
+"and note text. Verified finite appointment series retain their recurrence "
+"dates and deleted exceptions. Direct contact-group memberships, contact "
+"categories and known Work/Home/fax phone contexts are retained. Basic "
+"planner spans and annual anniversaries are retained; one-off anniversaries "
+"become all-day appointments, call and web records become text notes. "
+"Unsupported entries, layout, attachments and alarms are not transferred. "
+"Read the import report. For CSV, export each desired section in Lotus using "
+"File → Export → Delimited ASCII/CSV, then import each file separately. The "
+"original is read only. The file limit is 32 MiB; ZIP imports also have entry"
+" and size limits.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p>Ouvrez paramètres → importation → <b>Lotus Organizer (.or6 / .csv) …</b> "
+"et choisissez un fichier OR6 ou CSV. OR6 reprend rendez-vous, tâches, "
+"contacts et texte des notes. Les séries finies vérifiées conservent leurs "
+"dates de récurrence et exceptions supprimées. Les appartenances directes aux"
+" groupes, catégories de contacts et types de téléphone "
+"professionnels/privés/fax connus sont conservés. Les périodes simples du "
+"planificateur et les anniversaires annuels sont conservés ; les "
+"anniversaires uniques deviennent des rendez-vous sur la journée, les appels "
+"et entrées web des notes textuelles. Les entrées non prises en charge, la "
+"mise en page, les pièces jointes et les alarmes ne sont pas transférées. "
+"Consultez le rapport d’importation. Pour CSV, exportez chaque section dans "
+"Lotus via Fichier → Exporter → ASCII délimité/CSV, puis importez les "
+"fichiers séparément. L’original est seulement lu. Limite : 32 Mio ; les ZIP "
+"ont aussi des limites par entrée et de taille totale.</p>"
