+"require that service’s own application.</p><h3>Linux: Receive folders for "
+"photos and videos</h3><p>With your own Magnolie Notes phone connected over "
+"Wi-Fi, open <b>Settings ▸ Magnolie Notes phone connection ▸ Advanced "
+"functions ▸ Photos and videos</b>. No folder selection is needed before "
+"switching on synchronization. By default, photos go to <i>Pictures/&lt;phone "
+"name&gt;-Fotos</i> in your system’s Pictures folder. If you separately "
+"enable <b>Also synchronize videos</b>, videos use <i>Videos/&lt;phone "
+"name&gt;-Videos</i> in your system’s Videos folder. The video option starts "
+"off.</p><p>Choose <b>Photos · Destination folder</b> or <b>Videos · "
+"Destination folder</b> only to use a different folder for that media type. "
+"Leave the corresponding switch off while choosing. The folder must belong to "
+"you and not be writable by other users, including via a group. If the "
+"standard path is rejected, the Organizer does not change permissions or "
+"switch to another folder on its own. Choosing another folder alone does not "
+"grant Android media access, transfer or move files, or activate "
+"synchronization.</p><p>When shared media settings are available, their on/"
+"off switch is in the <b>Photos and videos</b> heading. Opening the section "
+"does not turn anything on. The local <b>Receive · Photos</b> permission is "
+"separate inside the section.</p><p>After opening an already saved book, you "
+"do not need to save it again just to choose a folder.</p><p>On Linux and "
+"Windows, a new default destination uses your account name only when the "
+"phone name is missing. If the phone name is just an emoji, for example, the "
+"default folders are <i>Telefon-Fotos</i> and <i>Telefon-Videos</i>. Already "
+"saved destination folders stay unchanged.</p><p><b>Restore</b> is under "
+"<b>Photos and videos</b>, after the destination folders and before "
+"<b>Synchronize now</b>. Local media versions can be restored without an "
+"active phone connection. On Linux and Windows, this section shows the same "
+"recycle-bin policy as under Security. For example, choose 30 days or "
+"<b>never – empty manually</b>. Your existing choice is preserved. Switching "
+"the recycle bin off does not empty it. Use <b>Delete permanently</b> for one "
+"entry. <b>Empty recycle bin</b> asks you to confirm the number of all "
+"eligible media items in the displayed local bin; on Windows, choose <b>Read "
+"media recycle bin</b> first. Originals not yet moved into the bin are kept. "
+"If emptying fails, refresh the list first; some items may already have been "
+"deleted.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, <b>Advanced functions</b> is only shown "
+"while Notes is connected over Wi-Fi. Without that connection, look for "
+"<b>Restore media</b> separately under <b>Magnolie Notes phone connection</"
+"b>; on Windows it appears for a paired device with a local backup.</p><p>In "
+"Magnolie Notes, <b>Restore</b> is under <b>Advanced functions ▸ Photos and "
+"videos</b> when connected over Wi-Fi. Existing local copies remain available "
+"in the Journal even when disconnected. Your gallery app manages the recycle "
+"bin for phone originals and its retention period (for example, 30 days). "
+"Empty that bin in the gallery app, not in the list of recovery copies in "
+"Notes.</p><p>Contact synchronization adds messenger destinations. The same "
+"WhatsApp or Signal number is not added again for that service, even if "
+"formatted differently. The same applies to a matching Threema ID. Existing "
+"formatting and custom actions are kept; different numbers, IDs and services "
+"remain separate.</p><p>Drawing tablet: KDE Connect sends position, contact, "
+"pressure and Pen/Rubber changes. Magnolie uses these in the active sheet, "
+"including the Notes drawing dialog. The visible hover cursor leaves no "
+"stroke and is not saved or exported. The phone menu offers fullscreen and "
+"settings to hide the finger-drawing button or place it in any corner. Pen "
+"variants, shapes, selection, zoom and undo belong to Magnolie’s toolbar. "
+"Tilt, pen rotation and extra pen buttons are not part of this KDE protocol.</"
+"p>"
