 #, no-javascript-format
 msgid ""
 "<p>Open a note or task and tap Print to use its current draft. Android "
@@ -14093,3 +13944,340 @@ msgstr "关于本项目"
 #. Complete versus partial snapshot restoration, Refs #824.
 msgid "<p class='achtung'><b>All always uses the replace method.</b> Changes made after the selected snapshot are overwritten and entries added later are removed. The additive method is available only for individual areas.</p>"
 msgstr "<p class='achtung'><b>“全部”始终使用替换方式。</b>所选快照之后的修改会被覆盖，之后新增的条目会被删除。补充恢复方式仅适用于单独选择的区域。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: android-apk-transfer, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<div class='download-karten'><figure class='download-karte'><a "
+"href='https://gitlab.com/maik3531/mint-forgs/-/raw/main/Magnolie-"
+"Organitzer/Magnolie-Notes.apk'><img class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='Magnolie Notes'><figcaption><b>Magnolie Notes</b><br>Magnolie-"
+"Notes.apk<br>gitlab.com</figcaption></a></figure><figure class='download-"
+"karte'><a "
+"href='https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.kde.kdeconnect_tp'><img"
+" class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='KDE Connect'><figcaption><b>KDE Connect</b><br>Google "
+"Play</figcaption></a></figure></div><p><a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>Magnolie"
+" Notes · F-Droid</a></p><p>Alternatively, install and update Notes through "
+"the F-Droid client. F-Droid recommends its client: downloading an APK from "
+"its website alone provides no update notifications and is less secure. The "
+"APK transfer and checksum steps above describe the direct project download, "
+"not F-Droid. Versions and signing certificates can differ between channels. "
+"Back up your data before changing channels; do not uninstall an existing app"
+" to bypass a signature mismatch.</p><p>In the prepared Notes update, About "
+"refers recognized F-Droid installations and F-Droid builds to the client "
+"instead of offering a GitHub update. Android may not retain the installer "
+"information; a manually downloaded APK does not reliably identify its "
+"website. If recognition is unavailable, follow the conditional F-Droid "
+"reminder when that was your source. This recognition is not a signature "
+"check.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<div class='download-karten'><figure class='download-karte'><a "
+"href='https://gitlab.com/maik3531/mint-forgs/-/raw/main/Magnolie-"
+"Organitzer/Magnolie-Notes.apk'><img class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='Magnolie Notes'><figcaption><b>Magnolie Notes</b><br>Magnolie-"
+"Notes.apk<br>gitlab.com</figcaption></a></figure><figure class='download-"
+"karte'><a "
+"href='https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.kde.kdeconnect_tp'><img"
+" class='download-qr' "
+"src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,'"
+" alt='KDE Connect'><figcaption><b>KDE Connect</b><br>Google "
+"Play</figcaption></a></figure></div><p><a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>Magnolie"
+" Notes · F-Droid</a></p><p>请通过 F-Droid 客户端安装和更新 Notes。仅从网站下载 APK "
+"不会收到更新通知。版本和签名可能不同；更换来源前请备份，不要为了绕过签名冲突而卸载应用。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: maps-routes-and-messages, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>Choose the destination address</h3><p>If several destinations are "
+"available, <b>Map</b> opens <b>Choose an address</b>: select a home, work or"
+" other address on the card, or an address of a named emergency contact. "
+"Labels include the person and relationship. A missing linked card is not "
+"offered. A single destination opens directly. <b>Cancel</b> opens no "
+"destination and changes no contact data. Your map service, route setting and"
+" saved sender address under <b>Settings ▸ Contacts</b> still apply; a route "
+"needs your own address as its starting point.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>选择目的地地址</h3><p>有多个目的地时，<b>地图</b>会打开地址选择：请选择卡片的家庭、工作或其他地址，或具名紧急联系人的地址。标签包含人员姓名和关系。找不到被链接的卡片时，不会提供该选项。只有一个目的地时会直接打开。<b>取消</b>不会打开目的地，也不会更改联系人数据。<b>设置"
+" ▸ 联系人</b>中保存的地图服务、路线模式和发件人地址仍然生效；规划路线需要自己的地址作为起点。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: phone-pairing, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>Confirm once at the counterpart</h3><p>Enable the phone connection and "
+"open Notes and Organizer on the same Wi-Fi. Start pairing and select the "
+"intended device. Both screens show the six-digit code. Compare it and press "
+"<b>Codes match</b> only on the other device. The initiating device displays "
+"the code and offers Cancel; no second approval is needed there. A desktop "
+"invitation is confirmed in Notes; a Notes request is confirmed on the "
+"desktop.</p><p>Wait for the connected status. Existing encryption and finish"
+" verification remain in use. Choose synchronization, contact and phone-"
+"function grants separately. Bluetooth data requires supported hardware and "
+"OS permissions; Wi-Fi remains preferred, and call audio is "
+"separate.</p><h3>Pair again after removal</h3><p>If the desktop removes a "
+"connected pairing, Notes forgets that relationship too. If the phone was "
+"offline, accept a fresh pairing request for the same computer and compare "
+"the new code; no manual forgetting is required first. Cancelling before "
+"confirmation keeps the saved pairing. Completing renewal replaces only that "
+"computer’s connection data; notes, tasks and other saved computers "
+"remain.</p><h3>Scope and permissions</h3><p>Each Organizer binds exactly one"
+" pinned own phone through <b>magnolie-phone/1</b>. This is separate from a "
+"Magnolienbaum branch and from KDE Connect. Notes can keep several paired "
+"computers and selects one active computer. Wi-Fi is available on Linux and "
+"Windows. Supported devices can use RFCOMM manually; missing OS permission, "
+"hardware or radio access may instead report <b>permission_missing</b>, "
+"<b>no_hardware</b>, <b>disabled</b> or <b>os_restricted</b>. This data "
+"channel carries no call audio.</p><p>Device status, read-only selected app "
+"notifications, contact reading and call actions have granular permissions. "
+"Choose them explicitly; pairing alone does not enable them. Notes and task "
+"synchronization use their shared preferences, and automatic Wi-Fi mode stays"
+" Wi-Fi only.</p><h3>Developer options and Notes diagnostics</h3><p>In "
+"Settings → About, click the version number on the left ten times. The "
+"additional Developer options tab contains Keep a troubleshooting log, Show "
+"log and Disable developer mode. Disabling also turns off the optional log. "
+"In Notes settings, tap the installed version ten times, open Debug options "
+"and enable WLAN debugging. Read Notes WLAN diagnostics on the desktop reads "
+"the version and up to 128 technical connection events through the confirmed "
+"own phone’s encrypted Wi-Fi session. Both sides must allow device status. "
+"Disabling Notes developer mode revokes WLAN debugging. Bluetooth cannot read"
+" this report.</p><h3>Phone filesystem in the file manager</h3><p>Under "
+"<b>Settings → KDE Connect</b>, <b>Phone name filesystem</b> opens the "
+"folders shared by the phone, using its actual name. The button appears only "
+"with a current confirmed Wi-Fi connection and available filesystem support; "
+"it disappears after disconnection, with Bluetooth alone or without a client."
+" Share storage locations in KDE Connect on the phone. The direct Linux "
+"connection needs SSHFS and fusermount; Windows needs existing SSHFS-Win and "
+"WinFsp. Existing system KDE Connect uses its own filesystem facility. The "
+"counterpart is checked again before opening.</p><p>Windows Setup offers the "
+"phone-filesystem components and, when needed, installs the bundled signed "
+"WinFsp/SSHFS-Win packages with one administrator approval. In the portable "
+"edition, run <code>filesystem-runtime/Telefon-Dateisystem "
+"vorbereiten.cmd</code>. Existing components are retained and are not removed"
+" when uninstalling Organizer. Reading status or opening the filesystem never"
+" installs components.</p><p>KDE Connect offers assigned music/video players "
+"and other active playback, including browser videos. In Settings → "
+"Magnolienbaum → Media players, Search/Open uses the system file chooser, "
+"separately for music and video. Linux also shows searchable titles/artists "
+"when the assigned player exposes MPRIS TrackList; Windows GSMTC exposes "
+"current playback, not a music library. The phone displays actual covers and "
+"optional shuffle/repeat when supported. Streaming-service catalog searches "
+"require that service’s own application.</p><h3>Linux: Receive folders for "
+"photos and videos</h3><p>With your own Magnolie Notes phone connected over "
+"Wi-Fi, open <b>Settings ▸ Magnolie Notes phone connection ▸ Advanced "
+"functions ▸ Photos and videos</b>. No folder selection is needed before "
+"switching on synchronization. By default, photos go to <i>Pictures/&lt;phone"
+" name&gt;-Fotos</i> in your system’s Pictures folder. If you separately "
+"enable <b>Also synchronize videos</b>, videos use <i>Videos/&lt;phone "
+"name&gt;-Videos</i> in your system’s Videos folder. The video option starts "
+"off.</p><p>Choose <b>Photos · Destination folder</b> or <b>Videos · "
+"Destination folder</b> only to use a different folder for that media type. "
+"Leave the corresponding switch off while choosing. The folder must belong to"
+" you and not be writable by other users, including via a group. If the "
+"standard path is rejected, the Organizer does not change permissions or "
+"switch to another folder on its own. Choosing another folder alone does not "
+"grant Android media access, transfer or move files, or activate "
+"synchronization.</p><p>When shared media settings are available, their "
+"on/off switch is in the <b>Photos and videos</b> heading. Opening the "
+"section does not turn anything on. The local <b>Receive · Photos</b> "
+"permission is separate inside the section.</p><p>After opening an already "
+"saved book, you do not need to save it again just to choose a "
+"folder.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, a new default destination uses your "
+"account name only when the phone name is missing. If the phone name is just "
+"an emoji, for example, the default folders are <i>Telefon-Fotos</i> and "
+"<i>Telefon-Videos</i>. Already saved destination folders stay "
+"unchanged.</p><p><b>Restore</b> is under <b>Photos and videos</b>, after the"
+" destination folders and before <b>Synchronize now</b>. Local media versions"
+" can be restored without an active phone connection. On Linux and Windows, "
+"this section shows the same recycle-bin policy as under Security. For "
+"example, choose 30 days or <b>never – empty manually</b>. Your existing "
+"choice is preserved. Switching the recycle bin off does not empty it. Use "
+"<b>Delete permanently</b> for one entry. <b>Empty recycle bin</b> asks you "
+"to confirm the number of all eligible media items in the displayed local "
+"bin; on Windows, choose <b>Read media recycle bin</b> first. Originals not "
+"yet moved into the bin are kept. If emptying fails, refresh the list first; "
+"some items may already have been deleted.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, "
+"<b>Advanced functions</b> is only shown while Notes is connected over Wi-Fi."
+" Without that connection, look for <b>Restore media</b> separately under "
+"<b>Magnolie Notes phone connection</b>; on Windows it appears for a paired "
+"device with a local backup.</p><p>In Magnolie Notes, <b>Restore</b> is under"
+" <b>Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b> when connected over Wi-Fi. "
+"Existing local copies remain available in the Journal even when "
+"disconnected. Your gallery app manages the recycle bin for phone originals "
+"and its retention period (for example, 30 days). Empty that bin in the "
+"gallery app, not in the list of recovery copies in Notes.</p><p>Contact "
+"synchronization adds messenger destinations. The same WhatsApp or Signal "
+"number is not added again for that service, even if formatted differently. "
+"The same applies to a matching Threema ID. Existing formatting and custom "
+"actions are kept; different numbers, IDs and services remain "
+"separate.</p><p>Drawing tablet: KDE Connect sends position, contact, "
+"pressure and Pen/Rubber changes. Magnolie uses these in the active sheet, "
+"including the Notes drawing dialog. The visible hover cursor leaves no "
+"stroke and is not saved or exported. The phone menu offers fullscreen and "
+"settings to hide the finger-drawing button or place it in any corner. Pen "
+"variants, shapes, selection, zoom and undo belong to Magnolie’s toolbar. "
+"Tilt, pen rotation and extra pen buttons are not part of this KDE "
+"protocol.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>仅在另一台设备上确认一次</h3><p>启用连接，在同一Wi-"
+"Fi中打开Notes和Organizer。发起配对并选择设备。比较两屏的六位数字，仅在另一台设备上确认一致：电脑邀请在Notes确认，Notes请求在电脑确认。发起端只显示代码和取消。等待已连接状态；权限另行选择。</p><p>通过已认证连接移除配对时，Notes也会移除该配对。手机若离线，可直接接受同一电脑的新请求，无须先手动忘记旧配对。确认前取消会保留旧配对；完成更新不会删除笔记、任务或其他电脑。Bluetooth需要受支持的设备和系统权限，不传输通话音频。</p><h3>开发者选项与Notes诊断</h3><p>在设置"
+" → "
+"关于中，点击左侧版本号十次。新增开发者标签包含故障排查日志、查看日志和停用开发者模式。停用也会停止可选日志。在Notes设置中点击已安装版本十次，打开调试选项并启用Wi-"
+"Fi调试。电脑端Notes诊断通过与已确认的本人手机之间的加密Wi-"
+"Fi会话读取版本及最多128条技术事件。双方都必须允许设备状态。停用Notes开发者模式会撤销Wi-"
+"Fi调试。Bluetooth不能读取此报告。</p><h3>手机文件</h3><p>在<b>设置 → KDE "
+"Connect</b>中，文件系统按钮显示手机的真实名称，并在文件管理器中打开共享文件夹。仅在已确认的Wi-"
+"Fi连接有效且功能可用时显示。断开连接、只有Bluetooth或缺少客户端时隐藏。请在手机的KDE "
+"Connect中授权文件夹。Linux直接连接需要SSHFS和fusermount；Windows需要SSHFS-Win和WinFsp。系统KDE "
+"Connect使用自身功能。打开前会再次验证设备。</p><p>Windows 安装程序提供手机文件系统组件，并在需要时经一次管理员授权安装随附的已签名"
+" WinFsp/SSHFS-Win 软件包。便携版请运行 <code>filesystem-runtime/Telefon-Dateisystem "
+"vorbereiten.cmd</code>。现有组件会保留，卸载 Organizer "
+"时也不会删除。读取状态或打开文件不会安装组件。</p><p>KDE Connect提供指定播放器及其他当前播放，包括浏览器视频。在设置 → "
+"Magnolienbaum → 媒体播放器中，搜索/打开会分别为音乐和视频打开系统文件选择器。Linux在播放器提供MPRIS "
+"TrackList时还支持标题/艺人搜索；Windows "
+"GSMTC仅提供当前播放，不提供媒体库。手机会显示实际封面及受支持的随机、循环功能。流媒体服务目录需在相应应用中搜索。</p><h3>Linux: "
+"Receive folders for photos and videos</h3><p>With your own Magnolie Notes "
+"phone connected over Wi-Fi, open <b>Settings ▸ Magnolie Notes phone "
+"connection ▸ Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b>. No folder selection"
+" is needed before switching on synchronization. By default, photos go to "
+"<i>Pictures/&lt;phone name&gt;-Fotos</i> in your system’s Pictures folder. "
+"If you separately enable <b>Also synchronize videos</b>, videos use "
+"<i>Videos/&lt;phone name&gt;-Videos</i> in your system’s Videos folder. The "
+"video option starts off.</p><p>Choose <b>Photos · Destination folder</b> or "
+"<b>Videos · Destination folder</b> only to use a different folder for that "
+"media type. Leave the corresponding switch off while choosing. The folder "
+"must belong to you and not be writable by other users, including via a "
+"group. If the standard path is rejected, the Organizer does not change "
+"permissions or switch to another folder on its own. Choosing another folder "
+"alone does not grant Android media access, transfer or move files, or "
+"activate synchronization.</p><p>When shared media settings are available, "
+"their on/off switch is in the <b>Photos and videos</b> heading. Opening the "
+"section does not turn anything on. The local <b>Receive · Photos</b> "
+"permission is separate inside the section.</p><p>After opening an already "
+"saved book, you do not need to save it again just to choose a "
+"folder.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, a new default destination uses your "
+"account name only when the phone name is missing. If the phone name is just "
+"an emoji, for example, the default folders are <i>Telefon-Fotos</i> and "
+"<i>Telefon-Videos</i>. Already saved destination folders stay "
+"unchanged.</p><p><b>Restore</b> is under <b>Photos and videos</b>, after the"
+" destination folders and before <b>Synchronize now</b>. Local media versions"
+" can be restored without an active phone connection. On Linux and Windows, "
+"this section shows the same recycle-bin policy as under Security. For "
+"example, choose 30 days or <b>never – empty manually</b>. Your existing "
+"choice is preserved. Switching the recycle bin off does not empty it. Use "
+"<b>Delete permanently</b> for one entry. <b>Empty recycle bin</b> asks you "
+"to confirm the number of all eligible media items in the displayed local "
+"bin; on Windows, choose <b>Read media recycle bin</b> first. Originals not "
+"yet moved into the bin are kept. If emptying fails, refresh the list first; "
+"some items may already have been deleted.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, "
+"<b>Advanced functions</b> is only shown while Notes is connected over Wi-Fi."
+" Without that connection, look for <b>Restore media</b> separately under "
+"<b>Magnolie Notes phone connection</b>; on Windows it appears for a paired "
+"device with a local backup.</p><p>In Magnolie Notes, <b>Restore</b> is under"
+" <b>Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b> when connected over Wi-Fi. "
+"Existing local copies remain available in the Journal even when "
+"disconnected. Your gallery app manages the recycle bin for phone originals "
+"and its retention period (for example, 30 days). Empty that bin in the "
+"gallery app, not in the list of recovery copies in Notes.</p><p>绘图板：KDE "
+"Connect发送位置、接触、压力和笔/橡皮切换，Magnolie将其用于活动画纸，也包括笔记绘图对话框。悬停光标不会绘图，也不会保存或导出。手机菜单可设置全屏，以及隐藏手指绘图按钮或将其放在任一角落。笔型、形状、选择、缩放和撤销属于Magnolie工具栏。此KDE协议不包含倾斜、笔旋转或额外按键。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: contact-details-and-anniversaries, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>Contact groups</h3><p><b>Settings ▸ Contacts ▸ Contact "
+"groups</b></p><p><b>More fields</b>: Family · Work · Client · Tradesperson ·"
+" Insurance · Doctor</p><p><b>Add contact group</b></p><h3>Exclude selected "
+"groups</h3><p>Open Settings → Notifications → Exclude contact groups. Choose"
+" Notifications, Anniversaries, Appointment overview or Print, then Birthdays"
+" only, All anniversaries, Appointments or All. Tick the specific contact "
+"groups: other groups remain unaffected. Each area keeps its own choices. "
+"Enable exclusions and save. For the overview, Also hide in the calendar is "
+"optional. Appointment rules use linked contacts; for synchronized work "
+"appointments without a contact, explicitly select their calendar. During "
+"vacation, you can suppress notifications while retaining the display, or "
+"hide the entries too. Print has separate choices, including contact cards. "
+"You can change or disable the rules at any time; disabling retains the "
+"choices. No contacts, appointments or provider data are deleted.</p><h3>Find"
+" a contact group</h3><p>Above the contact list, Contact groups offers All, "
+"No contact group and individual groups, including empty standard groups. A "
+"selected group searches across all alphabet tabs and combines with the "
+"search text. Selecting an alphabet tab returns to All and ordinary alphabet "
+"browsing. Filtering never changes memberships or provider "
+"data.</p><h3>Complete emergency contacts</h3><p>Under <b>More fields ▸ "
+"Emergency contacts</b>, add a named person and relationship. <b>Link "
+"existing contact</b> shows the current card’s details read-only: photo, "
+"company, phone numbers, email and postal addresses, dates, notes and social "
+"media. Edit the linked card to change them. Choosing <b>— do not link —</b> "
+"keeps the displayed details as an independent, editable copy. Changes in the"
+" editor apply only with <b>Save</b>; <b>Cancel</b> leaves the saved contacts"
+" unchanged.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>联系人分组</h3><p><b>设置 ▸ 联系人 ▸ 联系人分组</b></p><p><b>更多字段</b>: 家人 · 工作 · 客户 · "
+"工匠 · 保险 · 医生</p><p><b>添加联系人分组</b></p><h3>排除所选分组</h3><p>打开设置 → 通知 → "
+"排除联系人分组。选择通知、纪念日、日程概览或打印，然后选择仅生日、所有纪念日、日程或全部。勾选具体分组，其他分组不受影响。各范围分别保留选择。启用后保存。是否同时在日历中隐藏可自行选择。日程使用关联的联系人；对于没有联系人关联的已同步工作日程，请明确选择其日历。休假时可仅关闭通知，也可同时隐藏日程。打印有独立选择，包括联系人卡片。规则可随时修改或停用，停用时保留选择。不会删除数据。</p><h3>查找联系人分组</h3><p>联系人列表上方的联系人分组可选择全部、无分组或具体分组，包括空的标准分组。选中分组后，会跨所有字母查找，并与搜索文本组合。选择字母标签会恢复全部及普通的字母浏览。筛选不会更改分组关系或服务商数据。</p><h3>完整的紧急联系人</h3><p>在<b>更多字段"
+" ▸ "
+"紧急联系人</b>中添加人员姓名和关系。<b>链接现有联系人</b>会以只读方式显示该卡片的当前信息：照片、公司、电话、电子邮件和邮政地址、日期、笔记及社交媒体。需要更改时，请编辑被链接的卡片。选择<b>—"
+" 不链接 —</b>可将显示的信息保留为独立、可编辑的副本。只有<b>保存</b>才会应用草稿；<b>取消</b>不会更改已保存的联系人。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: welcome, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<h3>One page number, several screen sections</h3><p>A numbered handbook page"
+" may fill several screen sections, depending on your screen resolution and "
+"window size. Seeing the same page number again as you turn forward is "
+"intentional: no pages are missing or duplicated. The number identifies the "
+"fixed handbook page, so the contents and topic links always refer to the "
+"same page, even after resizing the window.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<h3>一个页码，多个屏幕区段</h3><p>根据屏幕分辨率和窗口大小，手册中一个有编号的页面可能分布在多个屏幕区段。向后翻阅时再次显示相同页码是正常设计，并非缺页或页面重复。页码代表固定的手册页面，因此即使调整窗口大小，目录和主题链接仍指向同一页。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: turning-pages-and-moving-around, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p class='kalender-blaettertasten'><kbd>&larr;</kbd> / <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> · "
+"Use the left and right arrow keys to turn one month, one week or two days, "
+"depending on the Calendar view. If a date or time cell has focus, the keys "
+"move focus instead. In text fields, they move the cursor.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p class='kalender-blaettertasten'><kbd>&larr;</kbd> / <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> · "
+"按左右方向键可根据日历视图向前或向后翻一个月、一周或两天。日期或时间单元格获得焦点时，方向键移动焦点；在文本框中则移动光标。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: the-appimage, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p>Magnolie Organizer is also listed in the <a "
+"href='https://appimage.github.io/Magnolie-Organizer'>AppImage catalogue</a>."
+" This is a catalogue entry; check the linked release and its checksum before"
+" running an AppImage.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p><a href='https://appimage.github.io/Magnolie-Organizer'>AppImage · "
+"Magnolie Organizer</a></p><p>Magnolie Organizer 也列在 AppImage "
+"目录中。运行前请检查链接的发布版本及其校验和。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: first-run-assistant, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p>On the phone-apps page, <b>Magnolie Notes · F-Droid</b> opens <a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>the "
+"F-Droid listing</a> as an alternative to the direct APK download. Opening "
+"the link does not install the app or grant phone permissions.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p><a "
+"href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>Magnolie"
+" Notes · F-Droid</a></p><p>设置向导的手机应用页面提供 Magnolie Notes · F-Droid 链接，作为直接 "
+"APK 的替代选择。打开链接不会安装应用或授予手机权限。</p>"
+
+#. Current rendered appendix: moving-from-lotus-organizer, Refs #827.
+msgid ""
+"<p>Open Settings → Import → <b>Lotus Organizer (.or6 / .csv) …</b> and "
+"select an OR6 file or CSV export. OR6 imports appointments, tasks, contacts "
+"and note text. Verified finite appointment series retain their recurrence "
+"dates and deleted exceptions. Direct contact-group memberships, contact "
+"categories and known Work/Home/fax phone contexts are retained. Basic "
+"planner spans and annual anniversaries are retained; one-off anniversaries "
+"become all-day appointments, call and web records become text notes. "
+"Unsupported entries, layout, attachments and alarms are not transferred. "
+"Read the import report. For CSV, export each desired section in Lotus using "
+"File → Export → Delimited ASCII/CSV, then import each file separately. The "
+"original is read only. The file limit is 32 MiB; ZIP imports also have entry"
+" and size limits.</p>"
+msgstr ""
+"<p>打开设置 → 导入 → <b>Lotus Organizer (.or6 / .csv) "
+"…</b>，选择OR6或CSV文件。OR6导入日程、任务、联系人和笔记纯文本。已验证的有限重复日程保留重复日期及已删除的例外。保留直接分组成员关系、联系人分类和已知工作/家庭/传真号码类型。保留基本规划时段和每年重复的纪念日；一次性纪念日转为全天日程，通话和网页记录转为文本笔记。不传输不支持的条目、版式、附件和提醒。请检查导入报告。使用CSV时，在Lotus中通过文件"
+" → 导出 → 分隔ASCII/CSV分别导出所需分区，再逐个导入。原文件仅被读取。单文件上限32 MiB；ZIP另有条目数量和大小限制。</p>"
diff --git a/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js b/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
index ad08aa7d525ead7e1a1edbc22deab4f1d9f17525..3742923cd4c1bc0630e40d44b55ba4a4f32e2c05 100644
--- a/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
+++ b/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ gettext("<b>Open Settings → Connections and scroll to Magnolienbaum.</b>");
 gettext("<b>Open Settings → Import.</b>");
 gettext("<b>Open Settings → Recovery and find Recovery journal below the trash.</b>");
 gettext("<b>Under Settings → Recovery, Create portable backup and Open portable backup use an independent archive password.</b>");
+gettext("<div class='download-karten'><figure class='download-karte'><a href='https://gitlab.com/maik3531/mint-forgs/-/raw/main/Magnolie-Organitzer/Magnolie-Notes.apk'><img class='download-qr' src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,' alt='Magnolie Notes'><figcaption><b>Magnolie Notes</b><br>Magnolie-Notes.apk<br>gitlab.com</figcaption></a></figure><figure class='download-karte'><a href='https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.kde.kdeconnect_tp'><img class='download-qr' src='data:image/svg+xml;base64,' alt='KDE Connect'><figcaption><b>KDE Connect</b><br>Google Play</figcaption></a></figure></div><p><a href='https://f-droid.org/en/packages/io.gitlab.maik3531.magnolienotes'>Magnolie Notes · F-Droid</a></p><p>Alternatively, install and update Notes through the F-Droid client. F-Droid recommends its client: downloading an APK from its website alone provides no update notifications and is less secure. The APK transfer and checksum steps above describe the direct project download, not F-Droid. Versions and signing certificates can differ between channels. Back up your data before changing channels; do not uninstall an existing app to bypass a signature mismatch.</p><p>In the prepared Notes update, About refers recognized F-Droid installations and F-Droid builds to the client instead of offering a GitHub update. Android may not retain the installer information; a manually downloaded APK does not reliably identify its website. If recognition is unavailable, follow the conditional F-Droid reminder when that was your source. This recognition is not a signature check.</p>");
 gettext("<div class='merke'><b>Do not confuse two contact routes</b>This page describes optional two-way branch synchronization, which can require Android read and write access. The one-time import on page <b data-page='android-one-time-contact-import' class='knopfwort'></b> is separate, read-only on Android, previewed, confirmed, and additive.</div>");
 gettext("<div class='merke'><b>Nextcloud is not the only DAV server</b>Magnolie 2.0.30 also accepts standards-compatible CalDAV and CardDAV services. Baïkal is supported for calendar, task, and contact synchronization; it does not thereby become a supported Magnolienbaum mailbox. See page <b data-page='dav-server-setup' class='knopfwort'></b>.</div>");
 gettext("<div class='merke'><b>One-time contact import is still not Personal Sync</b>Personal Sync continues to cover notes, notebooks, and own task trees. A separately confirmed Android contact import can copy contacts once without adding contacts to Personal Sync.</div><p>Only with both devices' explicit consent, Personal Sync shares read-only Custom tasks and appointments, including their own notes. Text blocks, linked text and attachments are excluded. Archives restore copies, not permissions.</p><h3>Automatic import: Notes → Organizer</h3><p>Update both apps. For each paired computer choose <b>Note synchronization direction</b>: <b>Two-way synchronization</b> or <b>Import Notes → Organizer only</b>. In Notes, the import switch is in Personal Sync within the phone connection; on the desktop, open the paired phone details. If either device chooses import, the effective direction is Notes → that Organizer.</p><p>Enable automatic Wi-Fi synchronization for the desired connection. Organizer must be running and unlocked to apply imports; operating-system background restrictions can delay connections. New notes and later phone edits retain their source identity, formatting, notebook assignment and supported attachments. Reconnecting does not create another copy.</p><p>A real conflict with an Organizer edit shows both versions. Choose <b>Keep (Organizer)</b>, <b>Apply (Notes)</b>, or cancel. Cancelling leaves the incoming change pending; manual synchronization or reopening the app allows another review. Organizer notes and changes are never sent back in import mode. Removing a phone note leaves its imported copy intact: note, notebook and attachment deletions are not synchronized in either direction. Tasks keep their separate settings. Changing the mode preserves existing content and waits for a fresh agreement with the peer; each computer keeps its own choice.</p><h3>Current simplified controls</h3><p>The earlier individual note/task switches on this page are replaced by automatic Wi-Fi synchronization or a manual start. A deliberate mode choice configures notes and tasks together; saved opt-outs remain until that choice. New pairings consider deletion proposals by default. <b>Skip deletions</b> is the optional exception, not permission to delete silently. Import mode still excludes note, notebook and attachment deletions.</p><p>Several computers stay paired; settings belong to the selected computer. The Custom option appears only when the desktop has its own tab. Magnolienbaum controls start collapsed and follow the desktop availability message; existing independent branches and pending received content remain accessible. Own phone identifiers need no additional application switch: Android permissions and restrictions still apply, and the permission button opens the required system request. While disconnected or searching, the calm status is <b>No existing connection</b>. The note editor offers tree sharing only when a confirmed recipient exists.</p><h3>Shared settings and the phone collection</h3><p>Notes and Organizer share the content, automation and skip-deletions choices. Change them on either side; the other shows the effective value. Time tracking is independent, and existing legacy one-way imports are preserved.</p><p><b>Only the Notes collection</b> updates personal notes and tasks present on the phone in both directions. Desktop-only entries stay on the desktop. <b>Skip deletions checked:</b> deleting in Organizer keeps the phone copy. <b>Unchecked:</b> the next synchronization removes the unchanged linked phone copy too. A separately edited copy is retained as a conflict. In manual mode, press Synchronize to transfer changes.</p><p>Deleting a phone copy in this collection mode removes it from automatic synchronization and preserves the Organizer copy. Right-click → <b>Send to Notes</b> can send it again later. This action appears only for entries not already present on the phone and is hidden in full-collection mode.</p><p>Choose a Notes symbol when creating a page. Its sending checkbox precedes the label and starts unchecked each time. Both day views use original creation dates; identical merged copies retain the older date. An untitled note displays its first content line.</p>");
@@ -22,12 +23,13 @@ gettext("<h3>AES-256-GCM</h3><p>Authenticated encryption used by Magnolie to kee
 gettext("<h3>Automatically dismiss anniversary reminders</h3><p>By default, anniversary reminders stay visible until you close them. This setting is independent of appointment reminders.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Bold, italic, underline, and strikethrough</h3><p>As soon as you start writing or select some text, a small row of four letters appears above the page: <span class='knopfwort'>B</span> <span class='knopfwort'>I</span> <span class='knopfwort'>U</span> <span class='knopfwort'>S</span>.</p><ol class='schritte'><li>Select the text: click before it, hold down the mouse button, and drag to the end.</li><li>Click <b>B</b> to make the text bold.</li><li>Click <b>B</b> again to remove the bold formatting.</li></ol><p>You can do the same from the keyboard: <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd> for bold, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>I</kbd> for italic, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>U</kbd> for underline, and <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>D</kbd> for strikethrough. When the cursor is in formatted text, the corresponding letter is highlighted.</p><h3>The spell checker</h3><p>Under <span class='knopfwort'>Settings ▸ Font</span>, select <i>Check spelling</i>. Misspelled words are then underlined in red.</p><p><b>Right-click</b> one of these words to open a sheet of suggested corrections. Click a suggestion to use it. At the bottom is <i>Add to dictionary</i>, for proper names that the Organizer does not yet recognize.</p><div class='merke'><b>The editing menu</b>Right-click to display Cut, Copy, Paste, and Select All. On a note page, the menu also contains the four formatting options. Suggested corrections appear only when you right-click an actual misspelling. This menu is also available in Magnolie text fields for links and for group and notebook names.</div>");
 gettext("<h3>Category colors for appointments and tasks</h3><p>Open Settings → Calendar → Category colors. Enter a unique category name, choose a color, and click Add. On an appointment or task, enter matching Categories and save. Separate several categories with commas or semicolons; the first category with a defined color wins. Custom color on the entry overrides that choice. Clear Custom color to use categories again.</p><p>Colored open tasks appear on their due date, or their start date when no due date exists, in Month, Week, Day and Planner. Planner preview, print and ODS retain the colors. Removing a color definition leaves saved categories and imported provider data intact. ICS files retain categories and the Magnolie-specific custom color; other programs may ignore that color.</p>");
+gettext("<h3>Choose the destination address</h3><p>If several destinations are available, <b>Map</b> opens <b>Choose an address</b>: select a home, work or other address on the card, or an address of a named emergency contact. Labels include the person and relationship. A missing linked card is not offered. A single destination opens directly. <b>Cancel</b> opens no destination and changes no contact data. Your map service, route setting and saved sender address under <b>Settings ▸ Contacts</b> still apply; a route needs your own address as its starting point.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Choose the type yourself</h3><p>The first field for a postal address or phone number is intentionally blank. The gray hints <i>e.g. Private</i> and <i>e.g. Mobile</i> are only examples and are not saved. Click the blank field to see all suggestions, or type your own label straight away.</p><p>For postal addresses, the available suggestions are <i>Address</i>, <i>Head office</i>, <i>Secondary office</i>, <i>Work</i>, and <i>Private</i>. You can also use your own labels, such as <i>Care unit</i>, <i>Holiday home</i>, or <i>Delivery address</i>. Enter the street, postal code, city, and country, if required, below the label.</p><p>For phone numbers, choose from <i>Landline</i>, <i>Mobile</i>, <i>Work</i>, <i>Private</i>, <i>Fax</i>, and <i>Pager</i>. Here too, you can type your own labels, such as <i>Reception</i>, <i>Care service</i>, or <i>Emergency</i>. Use <b>+ Phone number</b> and <b>+ Address</b> to add as many rows as you need; the minus sign removes only the corresponding row.</p><p>Email addresses work in the same way. The type field starts blank and displays the gray hint <i>e.g. Work</i>. Click it to choose <i>Home</i>, <i>Private</i>, <i>Work</i>, or <i>Other</i>. You can type your own label, such as <i>Club</i>, directly into the field. Enter the actual email address beside it. Use <b>+ Email address</b> to add further addresses.</p><h3>Anniversaries and other details</h3><p>Open <b>More fields</b>. The anniversary type also starts blank and displays only the gray hint <i>e.g. Birthday</i>. Click it to choose from all known types, including birthday, death anniversary, wedding anniversary, name day, and anniversary. Alternatively, type your own occasion. The entry is saved only when it has a date. If the year is unknown, enter only day and month; no age is calculated. Use <b>+ Event</b> to add further anniversaries.</p><h3>Emergency contacts</h3><p>In the same section, emergency contacts appear inside dashed borders. The relationship field has no default selection and displays the gray hint <i>e.g. Son</i>. Click it to choose options including son, daughter, carer, neighbor, or partner. You can type other relationships directly into the field.</p><p>Enter the person’s name and phone number below. Use <b>+ Emergency contact</b> to add as many people as you need; each has its own dashed border. Ordinary postal addresses no longer have this border. All emergency contacts remain visible on the contact card and are included when printing and exchanging data.</p><h3>Note, appointments, and tasks</h3><p>The <b>Note</b> is once again visible on the standard contact form rather than hidden under <i>More fields</i>.</p><p>Under <b>Appointments for this person</b>, the title starts blank and displays the gray hint <i>e.g. Doctor appointment</i>. Click it to choose typical appointments such as Doctor appointment, Meeting, Phone call, House call, or Authority appointment; you can still enter any title you wish. Use <b>+ More appointments</b> to add as many appointments as needed, including their dates and times.</p><p>The same applies under <b>Tasks for this person</b>: the blank field displays <i>e.g. Send documents</i> and offers Send documents, Errands, Call, and other typical tasks. Use <b>+ More tasks</b> to create multiple linked tasks. You can type your own titles directly at any time.</p><div class='merke'><b>Your custom labels are retained</b>When contacts are saved, exchanged as vCards, merged, or synchronized, your own labels are not replaced with generic ones.</div>");
 gettext("<h3>Confirm once at the counterpart</h3><p>Enable the phone connection and open Notes and Organizer on the same Wi-Fi. Start pairing and select the intended device. Both screens show the six-digit code. Compare it and press <b>Codes match</b> only on the other device. The initiating device displays the code and offers Cancel; no second approval is needed there. A desktop invitation is confirmed in Notes; a Notes request is confirmed on the desktop.</p><p>Wait for the connected status. Existing encryption and finish verification remain in use. Choose synchronization, contact and phone-function grants separately. Bluetooth data requires supported hardware and OS permissions; Wi-Fi remains preferred, and call audio is separate.</p><h3>Pair again after removal</h3><p>If the desktop removes a connected pairing, Notes forgets that relationship too. If the phone was offline, accept a fresh pairing request for the same computer and compare the new code; no manual forgetting is required first. Cancelling before confirmation keeps the saved pairing. Completing renewal replaces only that computer’s connection data; notes, tasks and other saved computers remain.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Confirm once at the counterpart</h3><p>Enable the phone connection and open Notes and Organizer on the same Wi-Fi. Start pairing and select the intended device. Both screens show the six-digit code. Compare it and press <b>Codes match</b> only on the other device. The initiating device displays the code and offers Cancel; no second approval is needed there. A desktop invitation is confirmed in Notes; a Notes request is confirmed on the desktop.</p><p>Wait for the connected status. Existing encryption and finish verification remain in use. Choose synchronization, contact and phone-function grants separately. Bluetooth data requires supported hardware and OS permissions; Wi-Fi remains preferred, and call audio is separate.</p><h3>Pair again after removal</h3><p>If the desktop removes a connected pairing, Notes forgets that relationship too. If the phone was offline, accept a fresh pairing request for the same computer and compare the new code; no manual forgetting is required first. Cancelling before confirmation keeps the saved pairing. Completing renewal replaces only that computer’s connection data; notes, tasks and other saved computers remain.</p><figure><img src='10-pin-abfrage.png' alt='Pairing dialog with a six-digit code and the match buttons'><figcaption>Confirm only when all six digits are identical on the computer and phone.</figcaption></figure>");
 gettext("<h3>Confirm once at the counterpart</h3><p>Enable the phone connection and open Notes and Organizer on the same Wi-Fi. Start pairing and select the intended device. Both screens show the six-digit code. Compare it and press <b>Codes match</b> only on the other device. The initiating device displays the code and offers Cancel; no second approval is needed there. A desktop invitation is confirmed in Notes; a Notes request is confirmed on the desktop.</p><p>Wait for the connected status. Existing encryption and finish verification remain in use. Choose synchronization, contact and phone-function grants separately. Bluetooth data requires supported hardware and OS permissions; Wi-Fi remains preferred, and call audio is separate.</p><h3>Pair again after removal</h3><p>If the desktop removes a connected pairing, Notes forgets that relationship too. If the phone was offline, accept a fresh pairing request for the same computer and compare the new code; no manual forgetting is required first. Cancelling before confirmation keeps the saved pairing. Completing renewal replaces only that computer’s connection data; notes, tasks and other saved computers remain.</p><figure><img src='11-stand.png' alt='Settings showing the paired phone, connection state and removal button'><figcaption>The status area names the paired phone, its availability and its fingerprint.</figcaption></figure>");
-gettext("<h3>Confirm once at the counterpart</h3><p>Enable the phone connection and open Notes and Organizer on the same Wi-Fi. Start pairing and select the intended device. Both screens show the six-digit code. Compare it and press <b>Codes match</b> only on the other device. The initiating device displays the code and offers Cancel; no second approval is needed there. A desktop invitation is confirmed in Notes; a Notes request is confirmed on the desktop.</p><p>Wait for the connected status. Existing encryption and finish verification remain in use. Choose synchronization, contact and phone-function grants separately. Bluetooth data requires supported hardware and OS permissions; Wi-Fi remains preferred, and call audio is separate.</p><h3>Pair again after removal</h3><p>If the desktop removes a connected pairing, Notes forgets that relationship too. If the phone was offline, accept a fresh pairing request for the same computer and compare the new code; no manual forgetting is required first. Cancelling before confirmation keeps the saved pairing. Completing renewal replaces only that computer’s connection data; notes, tasks and other saved computers remain.</p><h3>Scope and permissions</h3><p>Each Organizer binds exactly one pinned own phone through <b>magnolie-phone/1</b>. This is separate from a Magnolienbaum branch and from KDE Connect. Notes can keep several paired computers and selects one active computer. Wi-Fi is available on Linux and Windows. Supported devices can use RFCOMM manually; missing OS permission, hardware or radio access may instead report <b>permission_missing</b>, <b>no_hardware</b>, <b>disabled</b> or <b>os_restricted</b>. This data channel carries no call audio.</p><p>Device status, read-only selected app notifications, contact reading and call actions have granular permissions. Choose them explicitly; pairing alone does not enable them. Notes and task synchronization use their shared preferences, and automatic Wi-Fi mode stays Wi-Fi only.</p><h3>Developer options and Notes diagnostics</h3><p>In Settings → About, click the version number on the left ten times. The additional Developer options tab contains Keep a troubleshooting log, Show log and Disable developer mode. Disabling also turns off the optional log. In Notes settings, tap the installed version ten times, open Debug options and enable WLAN debugging. Read Notes WLAN diagnostics on the desktop reads the version and up to 128 technical connection events through the confirmed own phone’s encrypted Wi-Fi session. Both sides must allow device status. Disabling Notes developer mode revokes WLAN debugging. Bluetooth cannot read this report.</p><h3>Phone filesystem in the file manager</h3><p>Under <b>Settings → KDE Connect</b>, <b>Phone name filesystem</b> opens the folders shared by the phone, using its actual name. The button appears only with a current confirmed Wi-Fi connection and available filesystem support; it disappears after disconnection, with Bluetooth alone or without a client. Share storage locations in KDE Connect on the phone. The direct Linux connection needs SSHFS and fusermount; Windows needs existing SSHFS-Win and WinFsp. Existing system KDE Connect uses its own filesystem facility. The counterpart is checked again before opening.</p><p>Windows Setup offers the phone-filesystem components and, when needed, installs the bundled signed WinFsp/SSHFS-Win packages with one administrator approval. In the portable edition, run <code>filesystem-runtime/Telefon-Dateisystem vorbereiten.cmd</code>. Existing components are retained and are not removed when uninstalling Organizer. Reading status or opening the filesystem never installs components.</p><p>KDE Connect offers assigned music/video players and other active playback, including browser videos. In Settings → Magnolienbaum → Media players, Search/Open uses the system file chooser, separately for music and video. Linux also shows searchable titles/artists when the assigned player exposes MPRIS TrackList; Windows GSMTC exposes current playback, not a music library. The phone displays actual covers and optional shuffle/repeat when supported. Streaming-service catalog searches require that service’s own application.</p><p>Drawing tablet: KDE Connect sends position, contact, pressure and Pen/Rubber changes. Magnolie uses these in the active sheet, including the Notes drawing dialog. The visible hover cursor leaves no stroke and is not saved or exported. The phone menu offers fullscreen and settings to hide the finger-drawing button or place it in any corner. Pen variants, shapes, selection, zoom and undo belong to Magnolie’s toolbar. Tilt, pen rotation and extra pen buttons are not part of this KDE protocol.</p>");
-gettext("<h3>Contact groups</h3><p><b>Settings ▸ Contacts ▸ Contact groups</b></p><p><b>More fields</b>: Family · Work · Client · Tradesperson · Insurance · Doctor</p><p><b>Add contact group</b></p><h3>Exclude selected groups</h3><p>Open Settings → Notifications → Exclude contact groups. Choose Notifications, Anniversaries, Appointment overview or Print, then Birthdays only, All anniversaries, Appointments or All. Tick the specific contact groups: other groups remain unaffected. Each area keeps its own choices. Enable exclusions and save. For the overview, Also hide in the calendar is optional. Appointment rules use linked contacts; for synchronized work appointments without a contact, explicitly select their calendar. During vacation, you can suppress notifications while retaining the display, or hide the entries too. Print has separate choices, including contact cards. You can change or disable the rules at any time; disabling retains the choices. No contacts, appointments or provider data are deleted.</p><h3>Find a contact group</h3><p>Above the contact list, Contact groups offers All, No contact group and individual groups, including empty standard groups. A selected group searches across all alphabet tabs and combines with the search text. Selecting an alphabet tab returns to All and ordinary alphabet browsing. Filtering never changes memberships or provider data.</p>");
+gettext("<h3>Confirm once at the counterpart</h3><p>Enable the phone connection and open Notes and Organizer on the same Wi-Fi. Start pairing and select the intended device. Both screens show the six-digit code. Compare it and press <b>Codes match</b> only on the other device. The initiating device displays the code and offers Cancel; no second approval is needed there. A desktop invitation is confirmed in Notes; a Notes request is confirmed on the desktop.</p><p>Wait for the connected status. Existing encryption and finish verification remain in use. Choose synchronization, contact and phone-function grants separately. Bluetooth data requires supported hardware and OS permissions; Wi-Fi remains preferred, and call audio is separate.</p><h3>Pair again after removal</h3><p>If the desktop removes a connected pairing, Notes forgets that relationship too. If the phone was offline, accept a fresh pairing request for the same computer and compare the new code; no manual forgetting is required first. Cancelling before confirmation keeps the saved pairing. Completing renewal replaces only that computer’s connection data; notes, tasks and other saved computers remain.</p><h3>Scope and permissions</h3><p>Each Organizer binds exactly one pinned own phone through <b>magnolie-phone/1</b>. This is separate from a Magnolienbaum branch and from KDE Connect. Notes can keep several paired computers and selects one active computer. Wi-Fi is available on Linux and Windows. Supported devices can use RFCOMM manually; missing OS permission, hardware or radio access may instead report <b>permission_missing</b>, <b>no_hardware</b>, <b>disabled</b> or <b>os_restricted</b>. This data channel carries no call audio.</p><p>Device status, read-only selected app notifications, contact reading and call actions have granular permissions. Choose them explicitly; pairing alone does not enable them. Notes and task synchronization use their shared preferences, and automatic Wi-Fi mode stays Wi-Fi only.</p><h3>Developer options and Notes diagnostics</h3><p>In Settings → About, click the version number on the left ten times. The additional Developer options tab contains Keep a troubleshooting log, Show log and Disable developer mode. Disabling also turns off the optional log. In Notes settings, tap the installed version ten times, open Debug options and enable WLAN debugging. Read Notes WLAN diagnostics on the desktop reads the version and up to 128 technical connection events through the confirmed own phone’s encrypted Wi-Fi session. Both sides must allow device status. Disabling Notes developer mode revokes WLAN debugging. Bluetooth cannot read this report.</p><h3>Phone filesystem in the file manager</h3><p>Under <b>Settings → KDE Connect</b>, <b>Phone name filesystem</b> opens the folders shared by the phone, using its actual name. The button appears only with a current confirmed Wi-Fi connection and available filesystem support; it disappears after disconnection, with Bluetooth alone or without a client. Share storage locations in KDE Connect on the phone. The direct Linux connection needs SSHFS and fusermount; Windows needs existing SSHFS-Win and WinFsp. Existing system KDE Connect uses its own filesystem facility. The counterpart is checked again before opening.</p><p>Windows Setup offers the phone-filesystem components and, when needed, installs the bundled signed WinFsp/SSHFS-Win packages with one administrator approval. In the portable edition, run <code>filesystem-runtime/Telefon-Dateisystem vorbereiten.cmd</code>. Existing components are retained and are not removed when uninstalling Organizer. Reading status or opening the filesystem never installs components.</p><p>KDE Connect offers assigned music/video players and other active playback, including browser videos. In Settings → Magnolienbaum → Media players, Search/Open uses the system file chooser, separately for music and video. Linux also shows searchable titles/artists when the assigned player exposes MPRIS TrackList; Windows GSMTC exposes current playback, not a music library. The phone displays actual covers and optional shuffle/repeat when supported. Streaming-service catalog searches require that service’s own application.</p><h3>Linux: Receive folders for photos and videos</h3><p>With your own Magnolie Notes phone connected over Wi-Fi, open <b>Settings ▸ Magnolie Notes phone connection ▸ Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b>. No folder selection is needed before switching on synchronization. By default, photos go to <i>Pictures/&lt;phone name&gt;-Fotos</i> in your system’s Pictures folder. If you separately enable <b>Also synchronize videos</b>, videos use <i>Videos/&lt;phone name&gt;-Videos</i> in your system’s Videos folder. The video option starts off.</p><p>Choose <b>Photos · Destination folder</b> or <b>Videos · Destination folder</b> only to use a different folder for that media type. Leave the corresponding switch off while choosing. The folder must belong to you and not be writable by other users, including via a group. If the standard path is rejected, the Organizer does not change permissions or switch to another folder on its own. Choosing another folder alone does not grant Android media access, transfer or move files, or activate synchronization.</p><p>When shared media settings are available, their on/off switch is in the <b>Photos and videos</b> heading. Opening the section does not turn anything on. The local <b>Receive · Photos</b> permission is separate inside the section.</p><p>After opening an already saved book, you do not need to save it again just to choose a folder.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, a new default destination uses your account name only when the phone name is missing. If the phone name is just an emoji, for example, the default folders are <i>Telefon-Fotos</i> and <i>Telefon-Videos</i>. Already saved destination folders stay unchanged.</p><p><b>Restore</b> is under <b>Photos and videos</b>, after the destination folders and before <b>Synchronize now</b>. Local media versions can be restored without an active phone connection. On Linux and Windows, this section shows the same recycle-bin policy as under Security. For example, choose 30 days or <b>never – empty manually</b>. Your existing choice is preserved. Switching the recycle bin off does not empty it. Use <b>Delete permanently</b> for one entry. <b>Empty recycle bin</b> asks you to confirm the number of all eligible media items in the displayed local bin; on Windows, choose <b>Read media recycle bin</b> first. Originals not yet moved into the bin are kept. If emptying fails, refresh the list first; some items may already have been deleted.</p><p>On Linux and Windows, <b>Advanced functions</b> is only shown while Notes is connected over Wi-Fi. Without that connection, look for <b>Restore media</b> separately under <b>Magnolie Notes phone connection</b>; on Windows it appears for a paired device with a local backup.</p><p>In Magnolie Notes, <b>Restore</b> is under <b>Advanced functions ▸ Photos and videos</b> when connected over Wi-Fi. Existing local copies remain available in the Journal even when disconnected. Your gallery app manages the recycle bin for phone originals and its retention period (for example, 30 days). Empty that bin in the gallery app, not in the list of recovery copies in Notes.</p><p>Contact synchronization adds messenger destinations. The same WhatsApp or Signal number is not added again for that service, even if formatted differently. The same applies to a matching Threema ID. Existing formatting and custom actions are kept; different numbers, IDs and services remain separate.</p><p>Drawing tablet: KDE Connect sends position, contact, pressure and Pen/Rubber changes. Magnolie uses these in the active sheet, including the Notes drawing dialog. The visible hover cursor leaves no stroke and is not saved or exported. The phone menu offers fullscreen and settings to hide the finger-drawing button or place it in any corner. Pen variants, shapes, selection, zoom and undo belong to Magnolie’s toolbar. Tilt, pen rotation and extra pen buttons are not part of this KDE protocol.</p>");
+gettext("<h3>Contact groups</h3><p><b>Settings ▸ Contacts ▸ Contact groups</b></p><p><b>More fields</b>: Family · Work · Client · Tradesperson · Insurance · Doctor</p><p><b>Add contact group</b></p><h3>Exclude selected groups</h3><p>Open Settings → Notifications → Exclude contact groups. Choose Notifications, Anniversaries, Appointment overview or Print, then Birthdays only, All anniversaries, Appointments or All. Tick the specific contact groups: other groups remain unaffected. Each area keeps its own choices. Enable exclusions and save. For the overview, Also hide in the calendar is optional. Appointment rules use linked contacts; for synchronized work appointments without a contact, explicitly select their calendar. During vacation, you can suppress notifications while retaining the display, or hide the entries too. Print has separate choices, including contact cards. You can change or disable the rules at any time; disabling retains the choices. No contacts, appointments or provider data are deleted.</p><h3>Find a contact group</h3><p>Above the contact list, Contact groups offers All, No contact group and individual groups, including empty standard groups. A selected group searches across all alphabet tabs and combines with the search text. Selecting an alphabet tab returns to All and ordinary alphabet browsing. Filtering never changes memberships or provider data.</p><h3>Complete emergency contacts</h3><p>Under <b>More fields ▸ Emergency contacts</b>, add a named person and relationship. <b>Link existing contact</b> shows the current card’s details read-only: photo, company, phone numbers, email and postal addresses, dates, notes and social media. Edit the linked card to change them. Choosing <b>— do not link —</b> keeps the displayed details as an independent, editable copy. Changes in the editor apply only with <b>Save</b>; <b>Cancel</b> leaves the saved contacts unchanged.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Current SMS behavior</h3><p>The SMS button is available for numbers marked Mobile and for HOME numbers whose normalized German, Austrian, or Swiss dialing code is a known mobile code. Magnolie does not change the stored type. Fax, pager, and recognized landline numbers remain excluded. If detection is uncertain, edit the contact and mark the number Mobile.</p><h3>Assign the SMS action</h3><p>Right-click the contact card's <span class='knopfwort'>SMS</span> button to assign the action. <b>KDE Connect</b> opens the integrated conversation and local history. <span class='knopfwort'>System default</span> passes only an <b>sms:</b> address containing the number to the operating system. <span class='knopfwort'>Custom application</span> is available only on Linux and is not supported on Windows.</p><h3>Use the SMS sheet</h3><p>Left-click <span class='knopfwort'>SMS</span> to open the sheet. Choose the number, review the local conversation, enter the message, and send it. Each number has its own local history. Deleting local history does not delete messages on the phone; phone history may synchronize them again without replaying an old native notification.</p><h3>Status marks</h3><p>For incoming SMS, <b>●</b> means unread on the paired phone and <b>○</b> means read on that phone. This is not a receipt from the sender. For outgoing SMS, <b>◷</b> means queued, <b>✓</b> sent or accepted, <b>✓✓</b> is shown only for an actual delivery receipt, and <b>⚠</b> means failed. Classic SMS has no reliable recipient read receipt.</p><div class='achtung'><b>RCS is separate</b>RCS can provide delivery and read receipts, but KDE Connect's SMS interface does not expose complete RCS conversations or their receipt states. Google Messages uses proprietary RCS integration without an equivalent public interface for KDE Connect. Magnolie therefore never invents an RCS or recipient-read status.</div>");
 gettext("<h3>Current simplified controls</h3><p>The earlier individual note/task switches on this page are replaced by automatic Wi-Fi synchronization or a manual start. A deliberate mode choice configures notes and tasks together; saved opt-outs remain until that choice. New pairings consider deletion proposals by default. <b>Skip deletions</b> is the optional exception, not permission to delete silently. Import mode still excludes note, notebook and attachment deletions.</p><p>Several computers stay paired; settings belong to the selected computer. The Custom option appears only when the desktop has its own tab. Magnolienbaum controls start collapsed and follow the desktop availability message; existing independent branches and pending received content remain accessible. Own phone identifiers need no additional application switch: Android permissions and restrictions still apply, and the permission button opens the required system request. While disconnected or searching, the calm status is <b>No existing connection</b>. The note editor offers tree sharing only when a confirmed recipient exists.</p><h3>Read contacts directly from Notes</h3><p>Update both apps. In Notes select your paired computer and enable <b>Allow this computer to read contacts and photos</b>; approve Android’s contact-reading permission. The choice belongs to that computer. On the desktop, open Settings → Synchronization → Contacts (KDE Connect / Magnolie Notes) → <b>Import preview</b>. KDE remains preferred when available; otherwise the authorized Notes connection is used. Check each field before applying. Automatic photo retrieval changes no other contact fields and preserves manually chosen photos. Messenger entries come only from readable provider fields, never a guess from a phone number; private messenger profile pictures are not fetched. This read-only path does not change phone contacts and is separate from note/task synchronization.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>DAV server</h3><p>A server offering WebDAV-based services. Magnolie 2.0.30 can use a compatible CalDAV service for calendars and VTODO tasks and a compatible CardDAV service for contacts; Nextcloud and Baïkal are examples.</p><div class='merke'><b>CalDAV and CardDAV</b>These are open protocols, not Nextcloud-only features. Server-specific extras such as Magnolie's Nextcloud WebDAV mailbox are separate.</div>");
